{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "your-collection-id",
    "name": "NFTickets QR Testing",
    "description": "Test collection for NFTickets QR code flow",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080/api",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "apiKey",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "walletAddress",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "eventId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "tokenId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "contractAddress",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Generate API Key",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/apikey/generate",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["apikey", "generate"]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"walletAddress\": \"{{walletAddress}}\",\n  \"signature\": \"YOUR_SIGNATURE\",\n  \"message\": \"Generate API key for NFTickets\"\n}"
        },
        "description": "Generate an API key for authentication. You'll need to sign the message with your wallet first."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.environment.set('apiKey', jsonData.apiKey);",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Create Event",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{apiKey}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/event",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["event"]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Test Concert\",\n  \"description\": \"A test concert event\",\n  \"sectors\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"VIP\",\n      \"description\": \"VIP Section\",\n      \"capacity\": 100\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"General\",\n      \"description\": \"General Admission\",\n      \"capacity\": 500\n    }\n  ]\n}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.environment.set('eventId', jsonData.id);",
              "    pm.environment.set('contractAddress', jsonData.address);",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Issue Ticket",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{apiKey}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/event/issue-ticket",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["event", "issue-ticket"]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"eventId\": \"{{eventId}}\",\n  \"sectorName\": \"VIP\",\n  \"walletAddress\": \"{{walletAddress}}\"\n}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.environment.set('tokenId', jsonData.tokenId.toString());",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Get Token URI (Contains QR Data)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{apiKey}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/event/token-uri/{{contractAddress}}/{{tokenId}}",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["event", "token-uri", "{{contractAddress}}", "{{tokenId}}"]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    console.log('Token URI Response:', JSON.stringify(jsonData, null, 2));",
              "    // The QR code data should be in the metadata",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Authenticate Ticket by Sector",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{apiKey}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/event/authenticate-ticket",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["event", "authenticate-ticket"]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"eventId\": \"{{eventId}}\",\n  \"walletAddress\": \"{{walletAddress}}\",\n  \"sectorId\": 0\n}"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Verify QR Code",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{apiKey}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/event/verify-qr",
          "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
          "path": ["event", "verify-qr"]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"qrCodeData\": \"REPLACE_WITH_ENCRYPTED_QR_DATA_FROM_TOKEN_URI\",\n  \"scannerWalletAddress\": \"{{walletAddress}}\"\n}"
        },
        "description": "⚠️ IMPORTANT: QR CODE DATA IS NOW ENCRYPTED ⚠️\n\nTo test this endpoint:\n1. Run the 'Get Token URI' request first\n2. From the response, find the qrCodeData (it's JSON stringified)\n3. The qrCodeData now contains ENCRYPTED ticket information\n4. Use the encrypted string directly in this request\n5. The server will decrypt and verify the QR code\n\nSecurity Enhancement:\n- QR codes now contain encrypted data instead of plain JSON\n- Only the server can decrypt the QR code content\n- This prevents tampering and provides better security\n- The encrypted data includes all verification info:\n  * Token ID, Contract Address, Event ID\n  * Event Name, Sector Name, Sector ID\n  * Ticket Owner (wallet address)\n  * Timestamp and Server Signature\n\n🔒 CONTRACT-LEVEL VALIDATION:\nThe contracts now throw specific errors:\n- \"Ticket already used\" - When attempting to use a ticket twice\n- \"Ticket not owned by sender\" - When wallet doesn't own the ticket\n- Token existence validation\n\n📋 POSSIBLE ERROR RESPONSES:\n- TICKET_ALREADY_USED (409) - Ticket has been used before\n- TICKET_NOT_OWNED (401) - Wrong wallet address\n- TICKET_NOT_EXISTS (404) - Token doesn't exist\n- INVALID_SIGNATURE (401) - Invalid server signature\n- AUTHENTICATION_FAILED (401) - General auth failure\n\nNOTE: You should pass the encrypted string as qrCodeData, not the decrypted JSON object."
      }
    }
  ]
} 